id: pmc-sonp
title: Require explicit tagged status evidence for incomplete SDK inputs
description: CodeRabbit CLI review of PR 188 found undefined equals undefined when an SDK input has no status and its document is absent from the tag. Require present tagged status evidence and keep Git resolution failures fail-closed with useful root context.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-10T09:33:10.651Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T09:43:14.582Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T09:43:14.211Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T09:43:14.211Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: A missing tagged document cannot match a missing input status; existing present-status behavior remains; non-Git roots raise contextual errors; complete release checks pass.
parent: pmc-3jq8
release: 2026.9.10
resolution: Absent tagged documents no longer match missing SDK input statuses; Git root resolution errors include the requested root and underlying failure.
expected_result: "Only present matching tag evidence establishes membership, and Git failures remain actionable without silently falling back to timestamp attribution."
actual_result: The canonical PM-linked release gate passed all 476 tests with exact measured coverage and every release check; initial logic/context regressions and the separate host quota failure are preserved.
